[Annotator "GM Daniel Naroditsky and GM Ben Finegold videos"]
[Orientation "white"]
[Opening "Slav Defense: Chebanenko Variation"]
[SourceTitle "Slav Defense: a6 Chebanenko Variation"]
[SourceURL "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YX5bLrN2Yxo"]

1. Nf3 d5
2. d4 Nf6
3. c4 c6
4. Nc3 a6
{Chebanenko. Finegold's practical reminder: Black wants `...dxc4` and `...b5`; know your antidote.}
5. c5
{Weak-deck Advance System. Gain space and make `...b5` less simple.}
(5. a4
{Finegold's personal preference against `...a6`: if Black wants `...b5`, stop it directly.}
5... e6
6. Bg5
{Use the inserted `a4/a6` moves to make queenside expansion harder for Black.})
5... Bf5
6. Bf4
{Weak-deck reference after `c5`. Develop before launching pawn storms.}
6... e6
7. e3 Nbd7
8. h3
{Plan: keep the center closed enough to finish development, prepare b4 or Be2, and watch for the moment when Black's `...b6` or `...e5` break can be met by taking and using the c-file.} *
